# JavaScript Standards

- Use JavaScript (ES6+) only. Never add TypeScript, JSDoc-as-types systems, or `.ts`/`.tsx` files.
- Use ES modules (`import` / `export`). Prefer named exports; default-export React pages/layouts only when Next.js requires it.
- Use `const` / `let`. Never `var`. Prefer `async`/`await` over raw promises.
- Use `jsconfig.json` for path aliases. Never add `tsconfig.json`.
- Validate external input (API payloads, forms) with Zod at the boundary when validation is added.
- Handle errors explicitly; do not swallow them.

```javascript
// ❌ BAD
async function loadOrders() {
  try {
    return await api.get("/orders");
  } catch (e) {}
}

// ✅ GOOD
async function loadOrders() {
  try {
    return await api.get("/orders");
  } catch (error) {
    throw error;
  }
}
```
